{"nota":"Diccionario ES→EN. El inglés se genera con tools\\i18n.ps1 generar; no editar el .en.js a mano. keep: textos que no se traducen.","lit":{"\u0027 · ADN: \u0027":"\" · DNA: \"","\u0027¿Qué se separa en la anafase I de la meiosis?\u0027":"\"What separates in anaphase I of meiosis?\"","\u0027\u003c/div\u003e\u003cdiv class=\"eqline\"\u003e\u003csmall\u003eCélulas resultantes\u003c/small\u003e\u0027":"\"\u003c/div\u003e\u003cdiv class=\\\"eqline\\\"\u003e\u003csmall\u003eResulting cells\u003c/small\u003e\"","\u0027\u003c/div\u003e\u003cdiv class=\"eqline\"\u003e\u003csmall\u003eVariabilidad\u003c/small\u003e\u0027":"\"\u003c/div\u003e\u003cdiv class=\\\"eqline\\\"\u003e\u003csmall\u003eVariability\u003c/small\u003e\"","\u0027\u003cdiv class=\"calc-step\"\u003e2 · Segregación independiente\u003c/div\u003e\u003ctable class=\"calc-table\"\u003e\u0027":"\"\u003cdiv class=\\\"calc-step\\\"\u003e2 · Independent assortment\u003c/div\u003e\u003ctable class=\\\"calc-table\\\"\u003e\"","\u0027\u003cdiv class=\"card-kicker\"\u003eMitosis frente a meiosis\u003c/div\u003e\u003cdiv class=\"calc-step\"\u003e1 · Comparación\u003c/div\u003e\u003ctable class=\"calc-table\"\u003e\u0027":"\"\u003cdiv class=\\\"card-kicker\\\"\u003eMitosis versus meiosis\u003c/div\u003e\u003cdiv class=\\\"calc-step\\\"\u003e1 · Comparison\u003c/div\u003e\u003ctable class=\\\"calc-table\\\"\u003e\"","\u0027\u003cdiv class=\"eqline\"\u003e\u003csmall\u003eFase\u003c/small\u003e\u0027":"\"\u003cdiv class=\\\"eqline\\\"\u003e\u003csmall\u003ePhase\u003c/small\u003e\"","\u0027\u003cp\u003eAntes de dividirse, la célula pasa por la \u003cb\u003einterfase\u003c/b\u003e: \u003cb\u003eG1\u003c/b\u003e (crecimiento), \u003cb\u003eS\u003c/b\u003e (se replica el ADN) y \u003cb\u003eG2\u003c/b\u003e (preparación). Tras la fase S cada cromosoma consta de \u003cb\u003edos cromátidas hermanas idénticas\u003c/b\u003e unidas por el \u003cb\u003ecentrómero\u003c/b\u003e. En el modelo: \u003cb\u003e2n = 4\u003c/b\u003e (dos pares de homólogos: grande y pequeño; \u003cb\u003erojo\u003c/b\u003e = origen materno, \u003cb\u003eazul\u003c/b\u003e = paterno). El contenido de ADN pasa de \u003cb\u003e2C a 4C\u003c/b\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\u0027":"\"\u003cp\u003eBefore dividing, the cell goes through \u003cb\u003einterphase\u003c/b\u003e: \u003cb\u003eG1\u003c/b\u003e (growth), \u003cb\u003eS\u003c/b\u003e (DNA is replicated) and \u003cb\u003eG2\u003c/b\u003e (preparation). After S phase each chromosome consists of \u003cb\u003etwo identical sister chromatids\u003c/b\u003e joined by the \u003cb\u003ecentromere\u003c/b\u003e. In the model: \u003cb\u003e2n = 4\u003c/b\u003e (two pairs of homologs: large and small; \u003cb\u003ered\u003c/b\u003e = maternal origin, \u003cb\u003eblue\u003c/b\u003e = paternal). The DNA content goes from \u003cb\u003e2C to 4C\u003c/b\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\"","\u0027\u003cp\u003eDos fuentes de variabilidad: (1) \u003cb\u003esegregación independiente\u003c/b\u003e de los cromosomas homólogos: con n pares hay \u003cb\u003e2ⁿ\u003c/b\u003e combinaciones posibles (aquí 2² = 4; en humanos \u003cb\u003e2²³ ≈ 8,4 millones\u003c/b\u003e); (2) el \u003cb\u003eentrecruzamiento\u003c/b\u003e, que crea cromátidas recombinantes. Observa cómo cambian los colores de las cromátidas y qué combinación (rojo/azul) recibe cada gameto. Mitosis: clon; meiosis: diversidad.\u003c/p\u003e\u0027":"\"\u003cp\u003eTwo sources of variability: (1) \u003cb\u003eindependent assortment\u003c/b\u003e of homologous chromosomes: with n pairs there are \u003cb\u003e2ⁿ\u003c/b\u003e possible combinations (here 2² = 4; in humans \u003cb\u003e2²³ ≈ 8.4 million\u003c/b\u003e); (2) \u003cb\u003ecrossing over\u003c/b\u003e, which creates recombinant chromatids. Watch how the chromatid colors change and which combination (red/blue) each gamete receives. Mitosis: clone; meiosis: diversity.\u003c/p\u003e\"","\u0027\u003cp\u003eEn la \u003cb\u003eanafase\u003c/b\u003e se separan los centrómeros y los microtúbulos arrastran \u003cb\u003ecada cromátida hermana\u003c/b\u003e a un polo; a partir de ahí cada una es un cromosoma completo. En la \u003cb\u003etelofase\u003c/b\u003e se reconstruyen las envolturas nucleares y los cromosomas se descondensan; la \u003cb\u003ecitocinesis\u003c/b\u003e divide el citoplasma (en animales, por un anillo contráctil). Resultado: \u003cb\u003edos células hijas 2n, genéticamente idénticas\u003c/b\u003e, cada una con 2C de ADN.\u003c/p\u003e\u0027":"\"\u003cp\u003eIn \u003cb\u003eanaphase\u003c/b\u003e the centromeres separate and the microtubules pull \u003cb\u003eeach sister chromatid\u003c/b\u003e to a pole; from then on each is a complete chromosome. In \u003cb\u003etelophase\u003c/b\u003e the nuclear envelopes are rebuilt and the chromosomes decondense; \u003cb\u003ecytokinesis\u003c/b\u003e divides the cytoplasm (in animals, by a contractile ring). Result: \u003cb\u003etwo 2n daughter cells, genetically identical\u003c/b\u003e, each with 2C of DNA.\u003c/p\u003e\"","\u0027\u003cp\u003eEn la \u003cb\u003eprofase I\u003c/b\u003e los homólogos se emparejan (\u003cb\u003esinapsis\u003c/b\u003e) formando \u003cb\u003ebivalentes\u003c/b\u003e, y las cromátidas no hermanas intercambian segmentos en los \u003cb\u003equiasmas\u003c/b\u003e (\u003cb\u003eentrecruzamiento\u003c/b\u003e: variabilidad). En la \u003cb\u003emetafase I\u003c/b\u003e los bivalentes se alinean y la orientación de cada par hacia un polo es \u003cb\u003ealeatoria\u003c/b\u003e (segregación independiente). En la \u003cb\u003eanafase I\u003c/b\u003e se separan los \u003cb\u003ehomólogos\u003c/b\u003e (no las cromátidas). Resultan \u003cb\u003e2 células haploides (n)\u003c/b\u003e, con cromosomas aún duplicados (2C).\u003c/p\u003e\u0027":"\"\u003cp\u003eIn \u003cb\u003eprophase I\u003c/b\u003e the homologs pair up (\u003cb\u003esynapsis\u003c/b\u003e) forming \u003cb\u003ebivalents\u003c/b\u003e, and non-sister chromatids exchange segments at the \u003cb\u003echiasmata\u003c/b\u003e (\u003cb\u003ecrossing over\u003c/b\u003e: variability). In \u003cb\u003emetaphase I\u003c/b\u003e the bivalents line up and the orientation of each pair toward a pole is \u003cb\u003erandom\u003c/b\u003e (independent assortment). In \u003cb\u003eanaphase I\u003c/b\u003e the \u003cb\u003ehomologs\u003c/b\u003e separate (not the chromatids). The result is \u003cb\u003e2 haploid cells (n)\u003c/b\u003e, with chromosomes still duplicated (2C).\u003c/p\u003e\"","\u0027\u003cp\u003eEn la \u003cb\u003eprofase\u003c/b\u003e los cromosomas se \u003cb\u003econdensan\u003c/b\u003e, se rompe la envoltura nuclear y los \u003cb\u003ecentrosomas\u003c/b\u003e migran a polos opuestos formando el \u003cb\u003ehuso mitótico\u003c/b\u003e. En la \u003cb\u003emetafase\u003c/b\u003e los cromosomas se alinean en la \u003cb\u003eplaca ecuatorial\u003c/b\u003e, cada cromátida unida por su \u003cb\u003ecinetocoro\u003c/b\u003e a microtúbulos de polos opuestos. Es el punto de control del huso: no se avanza hasta que todos estén bien unidos.\u003c/p\u003e\u0027":"\"\u003cp\u003eIn \u003cb\u003eprophase\u003c/b\u003e the chromosomes \u003cb\u003econdense\u003c/b\u003e, the nuclear envelope breaks down and the \u003cb\u003ecentrosomes\u003c/b\u003e migrate to opposite poles forming the \u003cb\u003emitotic spindle\u003c/b\u003e. In \u003cb\u003emetaphase\u003c/b\u003e the chromosomes line up on the \u003cb\u003eequatorial plate\u003c/b\u003e, each chromatid attached by its \u003cb\u003ekinetochore\u003c/b\u003e to microtubules from opposite poles. This is the spindle checkpoint: the cell does not proceed until all are properly attached.\u003c/p\u003e\"","\u0027\u003cp\u003eLa \u003cb\u003emeiosis II\u003c/b\u003e se parece a una mitosis, \u003cb\u003esin replicación previa del ADN\u003c/b\u003e. En la \u003cb\u003emetafase II\u003c/b\u003e los cromosomas (aún con dos cromátidas, algunas recombinantes) se alinean en cada célula; en la \u003cb\u003eanafase II\u003c/b\u003e se separan las \u003cb\u003ecromátidas hermanas\u003c/b\u003e. Se obtienen \u003cb\u003ecuatro células haploides (n = 2) genéticamente distintas\u003c/b\u003e, cada una con 1C de ADN: las futuras gametos (óvulo, espermatozoide) o esporas.\u003c/p\u003e\u0027":"\"\u003cp\u003e\u003cb\u003eMeiosis II\u003c/b\u003e resembles a mitosis, \u003cb\u003ewithout prior DNA replication\u003c/b\u003e. In \u003cb\u003emetaphase II\u003c/b\u003e the chromosomes (still with two chromatids, some recombinant) line up in each cell; in \u003cb\u003eanaphase II\u003c/b\u003e the \u003cb\u003esister chromatids\u003c/b\u003e separate. \u003cb\u003eFour haploid cells (n = 2), genetically different\u003c/b\u003e, are obtained, each with 1C of DNA: the future gametes (egg, sperm) or spores.\u003c/p\u003e\"","\u0027«Contenido de ADN por célula» a lo largo del proceso y «Combinaciones por segregación independiente» (2ⁿ).\u0027":"\u0027“DNA content per cell” through the process and “Combinations by independent assortment” (2ⁿ).\u0027","\u0027«Proceso» cambia entre mitosis y meiosis, «Progreso (fase)» recorre las fases y «▶ Animar» las reproduce. En meiosis eliges la «Orientación en metafase I» y si hay «Entrecruzamiento».\u0027":"\u0027“Process” switches between mitosis and meiosis, “Progress (phase)” moves through the phases and “▶ Animate” plays them. In meiosis you choose the “Orientation in metaphase I” and whether there is “Crossing over”.\u0027","\u0027▶ Animar\u0027":"\"▶ Animate\"","\u00271 célula 4n\u0027":"\"1 4n cell\"","\u00271C por célula\u0027":"\"1C per cell\"","\u00272 células 2n idénticas\u0027":"\"2 identical 2n cells\"","\u00272 células n\u0027":"\"2 n cells\"","\u00272C por célula\u0027":"\"2C per cell\"","\u00272C por célula hija\u0027":"\"2C per daughter cell\"","\u00272n = 4 (bivalentes)\u0027":"\"2n = 4 (bivalents)\"","\u00272n = 4 cromosomas\u0027":"\"2n = 4 chromosomes\"","\u00272n = 4 por polo\u0027":"\"2n = 4 per pole\"","\u00272n → 8 cromátidas-cromosoma\u0027":"\"2n → 8 chromatids-chromosomes\"","\u00274 células haploides distintas\u0027":"\"4 different haploid cells\"","\u00274 células n\u0027":"\"4 n cells\"","\u00278 combinaciones\u0027":"\"8 combinations\"","\u0027Anafase\u0027":"\"Anaphase\"","\u0027Anafase I\u0027":"\"Anaphase I\"","\u0027Anafase–Citocinesis\u0027":"\"Anaphase–Cytokinesis\"","\u0027Avance\u0027":"\"Progress\"","\u0027Azul\u0027":"\"Blue\"","\u0027Azul grande ← · rojo pequeño →\u0027":"\"Large blue ← · small red →\"","\u0027C = cantidad de ADN de un genoma haploide. Mitosis: 2C→4C→2C. Meiosis: 2C→4C→2C→1C.\u0027":"\"C = amount of DNA in a haploid genome. Mitosis: 2C→4C→2C. Meiosis: 2C→4C→2C→1C.\"","\u0027Cada homólogo (con sus dos cromátidas) va a un polo.\u0027":"\"Each homolog (with its two chromatids) goes to a pole.\"","\u0027Cambia entre mitosis y meiosis, mueve el progreso o pulsa Animar. En meiosis puedes cambiar la orientación de los pares en metafase I y activar o no el entrecruzamiento.\u0027":"\"Switch between mitosis and meiosis, move the progress or press Animate. In meiosis you can change the orientation of the pairs in metaphase I and turn crossing over on or off.\"","\u0027células divididas\u0027":"\"divided cells\"","\u0027Células haploides con cromosomas de una sola cromátida.\u0027":"\"Haploid cells with single-chromatid chromosomes.\"","\u0027Células hijas\u0027":"\"Daughter cells\"","\u0027centrómero\u0027":"\"centromere\"","\u0027Cigotos posibles\u0027":"\"Possible zygotes\"","\u0027Combinaciones 2ⁿ (n = 2)\u0027":"\"2ⁿ combinations (n = 2)\"","\u0027Combinaciones por segregación independiente\u0027":"\"Combinations by independent assortment\"","\u0027Compara la meiosis con y sin entrecruzamiento: con él aparecen cromátidas mixtas rojo-azul.\u0027":"\u0027Compare meiosis with and without crossing over: with it, mixed red-blue chromatids appear.\u0027","\u0027Con\u0027":"\"With\"","\u0027Con entrecruzamiento\u0027":"\"With crossing over\"","\u0027condensación de cromosomas\u0027":"\"chromosome condensation\"","\u0027Condensación, ruptura de la envoltura nuclear y alineación en la placa ecuatorial\u0027":"\"Condensation, breakdown of the nuclear envelope and alignment on the equatorial plate\"","\u0027Contenido de ADN por célula\u0027":"\"DNA content per cell\"","\u0027Controles\u0027":"\u0027Controls\u0027","\u0027cromátidas separadas\u0027":"\"separated chromatids\"","\u0027cromosoma materno\u0027":"\"maternal chromosome\"","\u0027cromosoma paterno\u0027":"\"paternal chromosome\"","\u0027Cromosomas\u0027":"\u0027Chromosomes\u0027","\u0027cromosomas alineados en la placa ecuatorial\u0027":"\"chromosomes aligned on the equatorial plate\"","\u0027desactivado\u0027":"\"off\"","\u0027División celular\u0027":"\"Cell division\"","\u0027Divisiones\u0027":"\"Divisions\"","\u0027Durante la sinapsis de los homólogos.\u0027":"\"During synapsis of the homologs.\"","\u0027El contenido de ADN pasa de 2C a 4C.\u0027":"\"The DNA content goes from 2C to 4C.\"","\u0027El entrecruzamiento ocurre en…\u0027":"\"Crossing over occurs in…\"","\u0027el huso son los microtúbulos que salen de los centrosomas; la capa «Membrana y núcleo» muestra la envoltura que desaparece y se reforma.\u0027":"\u0027the spindle is the microtubules coming from the centrosomes; the “Membrane and nucleus” layer shows the envelope breaking down and re-forming.\u0027","\u0027En meiosis cambia la orientación en metafase I: los gametos reciben otra combinación de cromosomas rojos y azules.\u0027":"\u0027In meiosis change the orientation in metaphase I: the gametes get a different mix of red and blue chromosomes.\u0027","\u0027Entrecruzamiento\u0027":"\"Crossing over\"","\u0027envoltura nuclear formada\u0027":"\"formed nuclear envelope\"","\u0027Fase\u0027":"\"Phase\"","\u0027Fase S (replicación)\u0027":"\"S phase (replication)\"","\u0027Frontal\u0027":"\"Front\"","\u0027G1 → S (replicación del ADN) → G2: cada cromosoma pasa a tener dos cromátidas hermanas\u0027":"\"G1 → S (DNA replication) → G2: each chromosome comes to have two sister chromatids\"","\u0027Gametos (n = 2)\u0027":"\"Gametes (n = 2)\"","\u0027Gametos humanos (n = 23)\u0027":"\"Human gametes (n = 23)\"","\u0027Gráficos\u0027":"\u0027Charts\u0027","\u0027Huso\u0027":"\"Spindle\"","\u0027Huso y membrana\u0027":"\u0027Spindle and membrane\u0027","\u0027Interfase\u0027":"\"Interphase\"","\u0027Interfase (S)\u0027":"\"Interphase (S)\"","\u0027Interfase y duplicación\u0027":"\"Interphase and duplication\"","\u0027la citocinesis solamente\u0027":"\"cytokinesis only\"","\u0027la fase S\u0027":"\"S phase\"","\u0027La fase S se caracteriza por…\u0027":"\"S phase is characterized by…\"","\u0027la meiosis I\u0027":"\"meiosis I\"","\u0027La meiosis II se parece a…\u0027":"\"Meiosis II resembles…\"","\u0027La metafase se define por…\u0027":"\"Metaphase is defined by…\"","\u0027La mitosis produce…\u0027":"\"Mitosis produces…\"","\u0027La segregación independiente con n = 3 genera…\u0027":"\"Independent assortment with n = 3 generates…\"","\u0027las cromátidas hermanas\u0027":"\"the sister chromatids\"","\u0027Las cromátidas hermanas se separan y se forman dos células idénticas (2n)\u0027":"\"The sister chromatids separate and two identical cells (2n) form\"","\u0027Libre\u0027":"\"Free\"","\u0027los centrosomas\u0027":"\"the centrosomes\"","\u0027los cromosomas homólogos\u0027":"\"the homologous chromosomes\"","\u0027los nucléolos\u0027":"\"the nucleoli\"","\u0027Meiosis I\u0027":"\"Meiosis I\"","\u0027Meiosis I separa homólogos; meiosis II, cromátidas.\u0027":"\"Meiosis I separates homologs; meiosis II, chromatids.\"","\u0027Meiosis II\u0027":"\"Meiosis II\"","\u0027Meiosis: 1 célula 2n → 4 células n distintas.\u0027":"\"Meiosis: 1 2n cell → 4 different n cells.\"","\u0027Membrana y núcleo\u0027":"\"Membrane and nucleus\"","\u0027Metafase\u0027":"\"Metaphase\"","\u0027metafase de la mitosis\u0027":"\"metaphase of mitosis\"","\u0027Metafase I\u0027":"\"Metaphase I\"","\u0027Mitosis y meiosis\u0027":"\"Mitosis and Meiosis\"","\u0027Mitosis: 1 célula 2n → 2 células 2n idénticas.\u0027":"\"Mitosis: 1 2n cell → 2 identical 2n cells.\"","\u0027Mitosis: anafase y citocinesis\u0027":"\"Mitosis: anaphase and cytokinesis\"","\u0027mitosis: cromátidas · meiosis I: homólogos · meiosis II: cromátidas\u0027":"\"mitosis: chromatids · meiosis I: homologs · meiosis II: chromatids\"","\u0027mitosis: ninguna · meiosis: alta\u0027":"\"mitosis: none · meiosis: high\"","\u0027Mitosis: profase y metafase\u0027":"\"Mitosis: prophase and metaphase\"","\u0027n = 2 (cromosomas duplicados)\u0027":"\"n = 2 (duplicated chromosomes)\"","\u0027n pares de cromosomas (n = 2 en el modelo, 23 en humanos)\u0027":"\"n pairs of chromosomes (n = 2 in the model, 23 in humans)\"","\u0027ninguna (clones)\u0027":"\"none (clones)\"","\u0027Número de gametos posibles = 2ⁿ (sin contar entrecruzamiento). En humanos n = 23.\u0027":"\"Number of possible gametes = 2ⁿ (not counting crossing over). In humans n = 23.\"","\u0027Orientación en metafase I (segregación independiente)\u0027":"\"Orientation in metaphase I (independent assortment)\"","\u0027prácticamente ilimitado\u0027":"\"practically unlimited\"","\u0027Proceso\u0027":"\"Process\"","\u0027Profase\u0027":"\"Prophase\"","\u0027profase I\u0027":"\"prophase I\"","\u0027Profase I (sinapsis y entrecruzamiento)\u0027":"\"Prophase I (synapsis and crossing over)\"","\u0027Profase II / Metafase II\u0027":"\"Prophase II / Metaphase II\"","\u0027Profase–Metafase\u0027":"\"Prophase–Metaphase\"","\u0027Progreso (fase)\u0027":"\"Progress (phase)\"","\u0027progreso del proceso\u0027":"\"process progress\"","\u0027Punto\u0027":"\"Point\"","\u0027quiasmas: intercambio entre cromátidas no hermanas\u0027":"\"chiasmata: exchange between non-sister chromatids\"","\u0027Recorre la mitosis: las dos células hijas tienen los mismos cromosomas rojos y azules que la célula madre.\u0027":"\u0027Step through mitosis: both daughter cells have the same red and blue chromosomes as the parent cell.\u0027","\u0027replicación del ADN\u0027":"\"DNA replication\"","\u0027Reproducción clonal.\u0027":"\"Clonal reproduction.\"","\u0027Rojo\u0027":"\"Red\"","\u0027rojo = de origen materno, azul = paterno; el punto marca el centrómero.\u0027":"\u0027red = maternal, blue = paternal; the dot marks the centromere.\u0027","\u0027Rojo grande ← · azul pequeño →\u0027":"\"Large red ← · small blue →\"","\u0027rotura nuclear\u0027":"\"nuclear breakdown\"","\u0027Se separan cromátidas hermanas.\u0027":"\"Sister chromatids separate.\"","\u0027Se separan las cromátidas hermanas: 4 células haploides (n, 1C)\u0027":"\"The sister chromatids separate: 4 haploid cells (n, 1C)\"","\u0027Segregación independiente (2ⁿ) + entrecruzamiento = enorme diversidad\u0027":"\"Independent assortment (2ⁿ) + crossing over = enormous diversity\"","\u0027Segregación independiente: 2ⁿ gametos.\u0027":"\"Independent assortment: 2ⁿ gametes.\"","\u0027Separación en anafase\u0027":"\"Separation in anaphase\"","\u0027sí\u0027":"\"yes\"","\u0027Simulador 3D · biología\u0027":"\"3D Simulator · biology\"","\u0027Sin\u0027":"\"Without\"","\u0027Sinapsis y entrecruzamiento\u0027":"\"Synapsis and crossing over\"","\u0027Sinapsis y entrecruzamiento: sólo en profase I.\u0027":"\"Synapsis and crossing over: only in prophase I.\"","\u0027Sinapsis, entrecruzamiento y separación de cromosomas homólogos (2n → n)\u0027":"\"Synapsis, crossing over and separation of homologous chromosomes (2n → n)\"","\u0027sólo meiosis I\u0027":"\"meiosis I only\"","\u0027Superior\u0027":"\"Top\"","\u0027Telofase\u0027":"\"Telophase\"","\u0027Telofase I y citocinesis\u0027":"\"Telophase I and cytokinesis\"","\u0027Telofase II y citocinesis\u0027":"\"Telophase II and cytokinesis\"","\u0027Todos los cinetocoros unidos al huso en el ecuador.\u0027":"\"All the kinetochores attached to the spindle at the equator.\"","\u0027Tras la meiosis II, el contenido de ADN por célula es…\u0027":"\"After meiosis II, the DNA content per cell is…\"","\u0027una mit